        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-19T09:11:22Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): keep the .mch part tree as MachineTree\n\nparse_mch flattens kinematics.default.parts into Machine.axes and drops\nthe parent chain. A machine model needs the chain.\n\nparse_mch_tree reads the same JSON into a MachineTree: each part with its\nid, name, type, parent index and stated facts (travel, axis, pivot,\noffset, direction, spindle body, tool station), in mm. An axis that is an\nancestor of a head part is on the tool side; each other axis is on the\ntable side. A malformed tree refuses with the part id and the key.\n\nMachine, parse_mch and the existing checks do not change. rate, scale and\nmm_factor of parse.rs are now pub(super), so the two readers share one\nunit and unstated-limit law.\n\nFixes #2583\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
